ly) used are not freed.\n714:  */\n715: DLL_PUBLIC void daliReleaseUnusedMemory();\n716: \n717: /**\n718:  * @brief Preallocates device memory\n719:  *\n720:  * The function ensures that after the call, the amount of memory given in `bytes` can be\n721:  * allocated from the pool (without further requests to the OS).\n722:  *\n723:  * The function works by allocating and then freeing the requested number of bytes.\n724:  * Any outstanding allocations are not taken into account - that is, the peak amount\n725:  * of memory allocated will be the sum of pre-existing allocation and the amount given\n726:  * in `bytes`.\n727:  *\n728:  * @param device_id The ordinal number of the device to allocate the memory on. If negative,\n729:  *                  the current device as indicated by cudaGetDevice is used.\n730:  *\n731:  * @return Zero, if the allocation was successful, otherwise nonzero\n732:  */\n733: DLL_PUBLIC int daliPreallocateDeviceMemory(size_t bytes, int device_id);\n734: \n735: /**\n736:  * @brief Preallocates host pinned memory\n737:  *\n738:  * The function ensures that after the call, the amount of memory given in `bytes` can be\n739:  * allocated from the pool (without further requests to the OS).\n740:  *\n741:  * The function works by allocating and then freeing the requested number of bytes.\n742:  * Any outstanding allocations are not taken into account - that is, the peak amount\n743:  * of memory allocated will be the sum of pre-existing allocation and the amount given\n744:  * in `bytes`.\n745:  *\n746:  * @return Zero, if the allocation was successful, otherwise nonzero\n747:  */\n748: DLL_PUBLIC int daliPreallocatePinnedMemory(size_t bytes);\n749: \n750: /** @brief Returns serialized pipeline checkpoint\n751:  *\n752:  * Saves pipeline state together with provided external context.\n753:  *\n754:  * @param pipe_handle Pointer to pipeline handle.\n755:  *\n756:  * @param external_context External context to include in the checkpoint.\n757:  *\n758:  * @param checkpoint Output pointer to which checkpoint data should be saved.\n759:  *                   The buffer is allocated with daliAlloc, freeing it is caller's responsibility.\n760:  *\n761:  * @param n Output argument for checkpoint size in bytes.\n762: */\n763: DLL_PUBLIC void daliGetSerializedCheckpoint(\n764:   daliPipelineHandle *pipe_handle,\n765:   const daliExternalContextCheckpoint *external_context,\n766:   char **checkpoint, size_t *n);\n767: \n768: /** @brief Restores pipeline state from serialized checkpoint\n769:  *\n770:  * Should be called before running the pipeline.\n771:  * The pipeline needs to have checkpointing enabled.\n772:  *\n773:  * @param pipe_handle Pointer to pipeline handle.\n774:  *\n775:  * @param checkpoint Serialized checkpoint to restore from.\n776:  *\n777:  * @param n Size of the checkpoint, in bytes.\n778:  *\n779:  * @param external_context Output buffer to which checkpoint's external context will be saved.\n780:  *                         Populated fields of the external context can be later freed with\n781:  *                         daliDestroyExternalContextCheckpoint. Ignored if null.\n782: */\n783: DLL_PUBLIC void daliRestoreFromSerializedCheckpoint(\n784:   daliPipelineHandle *pipe_handle,\n785:   const char *checkpoint, size_t n,\n786:   daliExternalContextCheckpoint *external_context);\n787: \n788: /** @brief Frees all allocated fields of daliExternalContextCheckpoint\n789:  *\n790:  * @param external_context External context to destroy.\n791: */\n792: DLL_PUBLIC void daliDestroyExternalContextCheckpoint(\n793:   daliExternalContextCheckpoint *external_context);\n794: \n795: /** @brief Allocate memory.\n796:  *\n797:  * @param n Size, in bytes.\n798:  *\n799:  * @return Pointer to allocated memory or NULL on failure.\n800: */\n801: DLL_PUBLIC void *daliAlloc(size_t n);\n802: \n803: /** @brief Free memory allocated with daliAlloc.\n804:  *\n805:  * @param ptr Pointer to the memory buffer.\n806: */\n807: DLL_