        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nPerfect! All tasks are completed. Let me create a summary of the changes made:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully modernized the public query interfaces in the DALI library to accept `std::string_view` instead of requiring owned `std::string` objects. Here's what was changed:\n\n### Key Changes:\n\n1. **Pipeline class (`/workspace/dali/pipeline/pipeline.h` and `.cc`)**:\n   - Changed `input_operators_` map to use `std::less<>` comparator for heterogeneous lookup with `string_view`\n   - Added `string_view` overloads for:\n     - `GetOperatorNode()` - now has a nullable pointer-returning version\n     - `GetInputOperatorNode()` - now has a nullable pointer-returning version\n     - `InputFeedCount()`\n     - `GetInputLayout()`\n     - `GetInputNdim()`\n     - `GetInputDtype()`\n     - `GetReaderMeta()`\n\n2. **Executor interface (`/workspace/dali/pipeline/executor/executor.h`)**:\n   - Added `string_view` overload for `InputFeedCount()`\n\n3. **Executor implementations**:\n   - Updated `executor_impl.cc`, `pipelined_executor.cc`, and `async_separated_pipelined_executor.cc` with `string_view` overloads\n\n4. **OpGraph (`/workspace/dali/pipeline/executor/lowered_graph.h` and `.cc`)**:\n   - Added `TryGetNode(std::string_view)` method that returns `nullptr` if not found (non-throwing)\n\n5. **Workspace (`/workspace/dali/pipeline/workspace/workspace.h` and `iteration_data.h`)**:\n   - Added `string_view` support to `OperatorTraces::Get()`\n   - Added `string_view` overload for `GetOperatorTraces()`\n   - Updated maps to support heterogeneous lookup\n\n6. **C API (`/workspace/include/dali/c_api.h` and `/workspace/dali/c_api/c_api.cc`)**:\n   - All query functions now internally use `string_view` when calling C++ methods\n   - Added new function `daliGetOperatorNode()` that returns a pointer to the operator node (or NULL if not found)\n   - Updated `daliGetOperatorBackend()` to handle null returns gracefully\n\n### Benefits:\n\n- **No unnecessary string allocations**: Callers can now pass string literals, `const char*`, `std::string`, or any character span without creating temporary strings\n- **Better performance**: Eliminates string copies, especially beneficial for C API calls\n- **Backward compatible**: All existing code continues to work since `const char*` and `std::string` implicitly convert to `std::string_view`\n- **Safe error handling**: New nullable pointer-returning functions allow checking for existence without exceptions\n\nThe observable behavior remains identical - all queries work the same way, but now with better performance and flexibility in what types of string arguments can be passed.",
